  "title": "Audit & Optimize Seed Round Materials for Sustainability Investors",
  "content": "## Plan Overview\n\nThis plan audits and optimizes three core deliverables—pitch deck, financial projections, and demo—for a $1M seed round targeting sustainability investors. Since no files were attached, we first need to reduce uncertainty by researching what world-class sustainability seed rounds look like, then apply those benchmarks to produce actionable optimization guidance.\n\n**Approach:**\n1. **Reduce uncertainty first** — Research best practices for sustainability-focused seed decks, financial models, and demos from top investors and accelerators in the space.\n2. **Parallel deep-dive audits** — Once benchmarks are established, run parallel audits on each of the three deliverables.\n3. **Synthesize** — Combine all findings into a single prioritized optimization roadmap.\n\nSince no actual files were provided, the audits will produce detailed checklists, frameworks, and specific recommendations the user can apply to their materials.",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "goal": "Research best practices and benchmarks for $1M seed rounds targeting sustainability/climate/impact investors. Include: what top sustainability VCs (e.g., Lowercarbon Capital, Congruent Ventures, Breakthrough Energy Ventures, SOSV) look for in seed decks, common financial model expectations at seed stage, demo best practices, and any publicly available exemplary sustainability seed decks or teardowns.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Produce a comprehensive pitch deck audit framework and optimization guide specifically for sustainability seed rounds. Cover: ideal narrative arc (problem → market → solution → sustainability impact metrics → business model → traction → team → ask/use of funds), slide-by-slide checklist, common pitfalls with sustainability decks (greenwashing flags, missing unit economics, vague impact claims), design/visual best practices, and specific recommendations for targeting impact/sustainability investors. Reference benchmarks from Task 0.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": [0]
    },
    {
      "goal": "Produce a comprehensive financial projections audit framework and optimization guide for a $1M sustainability seed round. Cover: expected model structure (revenue model, cost structure, burn rate, runway calculation, use of funds breakdown), key metrics sustainability investors scrutinize (CAC, LTV, gross margin, carbon/impact metrics per dollar), common red flags at seed stage (hockey-stick without basis, missing assumptions, no sensitivity analysis), and specific templates/structures for a compelling $1M raise. Reference benchmarks from Task 0.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": [0]
    },
    {
      "goal": "Produce a comprehensive demo audit framework and optimization guide for sustainability seed fundraising. Cover: ideal demo flow and duration (2-3 min max), how to showcase sustainability impact visually, technical credibility signals, common demo anti-patterns (feature tours vs. story-driven demos), live vs. recorded demo tradeoffs, backup strategies, and how to tie demo moments to investor decision criteria. Reference benchmarks from Task 0.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": [0]
    },
    {
      "goal": "Synthesize all findings from Tasks 1-3 into a single, prioritized optimization roadmap. Structure as: (1) Executive summary of the biggest opportunities across all three deliverables, (2) Priority-ranked action items (High/Medium/Low impact) for pitch deck, financial projections, and demo, (3) Cross-cutting themes and consistency checks between the three materials, (4) A suggested timeline for implementing optimizations before investor meetings, (5) Quick-win checklist (changes that can be made in <1 day). Make the output actionable and specific.",
